 "findings": [
  {
   "effect": "Never a pass, and the zero count is right (no Popen event); but the docstring's rule and FAILURE-CAPTURE section 2's 'interrupted, therefore unknown' are not met, and the handler turns the signal into an ordinary exit 1.",
   "id": "TR2-01",
   "issue": "A KeyboardInterrupt (SIGINT, or SIGTERM or SIGHUP through the handler) raised in run_row before run_process leaves intent.json without outcome.json, and run() records the row as FAILED_BEFORE_START and PROVEN_ZERO without 'interrupted', so the run is ROWS_UNMET with exit 1. Raised inside run_process before Popen, it gives an outcome.json that says UNKNOWN and interrupted, which run.json contradicts.",
   "location": [
    "tooling/run_direct_probe.py:937-952 (per-row except in run)",
    "tooling/run_direct_probe.py:973",
    "tooling/run_direct_probe.py:825-835,884-885",
    "tooling/run_direct_probe.py:46-49 (docstring)"
   ],
   "recommendation": "Mark a KeyboardInterrupt or SystemExit in the per-row handler as interrupted (run UNKNOWN); keep the row's own outcome.json state when it was written; add a test that interrupts before a start. Until then S6 notes that any interrupted runner command is unknown by FAILURE-CAPTURE section 2.",
   "severity": "nonmandatory",
   "title": "An interruption before a row's start is not recorded as UNKNOWN"
  },
  {
   "effect": "None on the code; the other tests named for TR-02 and TR-03 fail for the defects (confirmed by my rerun).",
   "id": "TR2-02",
   "issue": "The ROW-TARGET part of test_bound_inputs_and_row_shapes_refuse_before_any_start fails with (2, 'ROWS') instead of (2, 'ROW-TARGET'): the rejected runner already refused a pre-existing supervisor output, under ROWS. The 'supervisor error not implied by the status' subtest fails because rows schema /1 has no such field; the row simply ran.",
   "location": [
    "tooling/tests/TEST-RUN-AGAINST-REJECTED-001.txt: header lines 16 and 19",
    "AUTHOR-NOTES.md section 6, rows TR-02 and TR-03"
   ],
   "recommendation": "Say so where S6 cites this evidence, or correct the header; no code change.",
   "severity": "nonmandatory",
   "title": "Two sub-checks listed against rejected-001 fail there for a renamed rule or a new field"
  },
  {
   "effect": "On the real files both are inert: all 61 .constructor( calls are new expressions (three.core.js 42, three.module.js 1, three.webgpu.js 12, BufferGeometryUtils.js 6); Reflect occurs only as Reflect.get in three.webgpu.js's proxies; the validator's five computed globals are dart2js's window[tag] lookups, which return null under Node.",
   "id": "TR2-03",
   "issue": "Neither the wider scan nor the frozen rule lists the Function constructor reached through a function's .constructor or Reflect.construct, nor computed members of globalThis, self or window; each can reach process or code from a string without any scanned name.",
   "location": [
    "tooling/scan_mc11.py:84-134 (PROCESS_CREATION, DYNAMIC, the frozen patterns)"
   ],
   "recommendation": "The S6 reviewed list's notes record both route classes and this cross-check under the stated limit; optionally list .constructor( without new, Reflect.construct and computed global members as dynamic hits for review.",
   "severity": "nonmandatory",
   "title": "Neither MC11 verdict flags Function reached through .constructor, or computed global members"
  },
  {
   "effect": "Fail-closed: nothing is sent that should not be; the readback can be incomplete without saying so, and a zombie cannot be told from an unidentifiable live process.",
   "id": "TR2-04",
   "issue": "os.walk runs without onerror, so an unreadable directory's entries leave the FC-K5 listing without a record. proc_pidinfo is called with argument 0; by XNU's source this flavor finds an exited, unreaped process only for a non-zero argument (not observed here), so such a process reads success from kill, EPERM from killpg and ESRCH from proc_pidinfo, and is recorded only as 'present, identity not established'.",
   "location": [
    "tooling/capture_probe.py:494-503 (directory_listing)",
    "tooling/capture_probe.py:303-312 (bsdinfo)"
   ],
   "recommendation": "Record walk errors; optionally read an unreaped process's facts with a non-zero argument and record its status, still sending nothing.",
   "severity": "nonmandatory",
   "title": "capture_probe.py: unreadable directories are omitted silently, and a zombie's facts are not read"
  },
  {
   "effect": "Measured in a -I -S -B process: every module those imports load is frozen or built in (36), an extension (8) or a source with cached bytecode (34), apart from my script's __main__; no write would occur today.",
   "id": "TR2-05",
   "issue": "A start without -B has already imported a tool's module-level imports (and, for discover and the collector, site's start-up) when the tool refuses; the refusal detects the mistake, it does not prevent it.",
   "location": [
    "every tool, for example tooling/capture_probe.py:48-58 (imports) and 533 (the check)"
   ],
   "recommendation": "S6 records that the refusal relies on the frozen framework's bytecode set; optionally check sys.flags.dont_write_bytecode in each tool's first statement.",
   "severity": "nonmandatory",
   "title": "The -B refusal comes after each tool's module-level imports, so it cannot prevent a write"
  },
  {
   "effect": "accounting_refused holds through the real code path, but the record's accounting refusal is not the 0.2.0 provider's accounting.",
   "id": "TR2-06",
   "issue": "After the real configuration change the configuration no longer matches the selected digest, so facade.finish_cpu_cohort is dispatched to the unchanged 0.1.0 code, which refuses with CH-SELECTION and a 0.1.0 refusal without the 0.2.0 labels; the attempt's refusal is v02's own _job, dispatched before the change.",
   "location": [
    "tooling/control_harness.py:751-753,780 (mc29)",
    "W5-PROVIDER section 4 (dispatch)",
    "CONTROLS-FROZEN.json F-07"
   ],
   "recommendation": "S6 states it in MC29's expected outcome: configuration case finish_error CH-SELECTION from the 0.1.0 code (F-07); job-input case CH-EVIDENCE from v02.",
   "severity": "nonmandatory",
   "title": "In MC29's configuration case the accounting refusal is the facade's 0.1.0 code's"
  }
 ],
